  "releaseNotes": "20260429.0.0 â€” Telemetry Phase 1 completion`r`n- Adds RTI-side telemetry hooks for subscription matching, attribute distribution, interaction routing, and runtime state sampling.`r`n- Adds telemetry host/runtime composition and end-to-end validation coverage with .fort generation.`r`n- Pairs with client-side telemetry and perf harness support for the Part 3 empirical validation workflow.`r`n`r`n20260426.0.0 — Transport thread-safety & Chat lifecycle fix\n- Serializes FP transport SendAsync via SemaphoreSlim (TcpFpTransport, TlsFpTransport, WebSocketFpTransportBase); concurrent NetworkStream writes were corrupting the FP frame stream and causing ResignFederationExecution timeouts.\n- Fixes Chat MainViewModel.OnLocalUserReady to propagate the simulation CancellationToken to UpdateAsync, preventing a post-disconnect UI-thread write from racing the background resign.\n\n20260424.0.0 — Complete Support Services coverage (IEEE 1516-2025 §10)\n- Full §10.2-10.60 coverage: handle lookup, handle normalisation, exception/advisory switches.\n- EnableCallbacks / DisableCallbacks delivery gating in FpCallbackWorker.\n- LBTS/GALT federation-scoped index + dirty-federation grant scheduling; TSO heap for O(log n) head inspection.\n- Typed HLA exceptions for invalid handles, unpublished send/update, duplicate time-mode enables, and out-of-order advance requests.\n- Retired legacy hla.proto and Fora.Core.Proto escape hatch.\n- 266/266 integration tests green.\n\n20260423.4.0 — DDM coverage (IEEE 1516-2025 §9)\n- RequestAttributeValueUpdateWithRegions and region-aware UnassociateRegionsForUpdates.\n- RegisterObjectInstanceWithRegions now preserves attribute-region associations in simulator routing.\n- Full §9.2-9.13 integration coverage.\n- Federation Management: Complete 4.2-4.35 coverage, save/restore status and abort services, and peer resign notifications.\n- Declaration Management: Complete 5.2-5.17 coverage, including subset unpublish/unsubscribe and directed-interaction variants.\n- Object Management: Complete 6.2-6.33 coverage, object instance name reservation/release, and transportation type change/query.\n- Ownership Management: Complete 7.2-7.19 coverage, acquisition-if-available, release denied, and divestiture-if-wanted workflows.\n- Time Management: Complete 8.2-8.26 coverage, including Flush Queue Grant and Change Default Attribute Order Type.\n- DDM: Complete 9.2-9.13 coverage, region-aware attribute updates, and interaction routing.\n- Support Services: Complete 10.2-10.60 coverage, including callback enable/disable delivery control.\n- Fixed enum mapping for federation save/restore status callbacks.\n- Extended integration test suite with 140+ new coverage tests.",
